<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site3.css?v=31"><!-- site3: injected per-page (perf) -->

<%# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    ABOVE-THE-FOLD COMPACTION — PHONES ONLY.

    Measured on the live page at 390x844 (iPhone 14), 2026-11-09:

        header        36   109    (the logo alone is 90)
        breadcrumb   145    44    (two lines — the product name wraps)
        gallery      205   557    main image 269 + thumbnail grid 288
        title        830   130    four lines at 30px
        PRICE       1000    48    <- 156px BELOW the fold
        ADD TO CART 1180   101    <- 336px BELOW the fold

    A shopper had to scroll about 1.4 screens to find out what it costs.
    The thumbnail grid was the biggest single offender: 288px, larger than
    the 269px image it serves, because it is a 3-column grid of square
    tiles and six thumbs make two ~114px rows.

    This block takes ~314px out of the fold on phones. The remaining ~45px
    is the logo, which is NOT here on purpose — see the note below.

    ⚠️ WHY THIS IS INLINE AND NOT IN site-bundle.css.
    The bundle is rebuilt by hand and the documented `cat` recipe does not
    reproduce it (main.ejs:178). src/utils/breakpoints.js records what that
    cost once already: `@media (max-width:480px){.site-nav{padding:0 12px}}`
    sat in site4.css while phones still rendered 40px of padding, because
    site4's storefront rules never reached the bundle. Settings-driven CSS
    on this site is therefore emitted inline in the page that uses it. It
    cannot go stale, needs no rebuild, and needs no ?v= bump.

    ⚠️ THE MEDIA QUERY IS NOT TYPED BY HAND. mobile_max is a Theme Editor
    setting; breakpoints.mq.mobile derives the condition so the +/-1 against
    the tablet band can never drift. Do not replace it with a literal.

    ⚠️ THE LOGO IS DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED HERE. .nav-logo is already
    settings-driven per band (header.ejs:121, logo_width_mobile /
    logo_height_mobile), and the nav bar height derives from it as
    max(64, logo+16). Hard-coding a height here would fight that system and
    desync the <img> width/height that reserve space against CLS. Shrinking
    the phone logo is a Theme Editor change, not a code change.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ %>
<% var _bpPdp = breakpoints.resolve(settings || {}); %>
<style nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
@media <%= _bpPdp.mq.mobile %> {
  /* ── 0. THE REORDER — BUY BOX COMPACTED BENEATH THE HERO ────────
     docs/mockups/mobile_pdp_current_vs_proposed.html, approved. Order is
     hero → badges → brand → title → price → availability → buy button →
     trust. Nothing is removed: the full gallery, variant cards, specs and
     description all still follow, in their existing order.

     ⚠️ THE HERO STAYS FIRST. The photo is what sells a $2,400 vanity, and
     an earlier attempt at this put price and button ABOVE the image. That
     was wrong and it was not what the mockup asked for — its note reads
     "hero 300→232px", i.e. keep the image and shrink it.

     ⚠️ display:contents IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT DECORATION.
     .detail-layout is a two-column grid whose only children are
     .detail-gallery and .detail-info. Everything we need to reorder lives
     INSIDE .detail-info, and `order` sorts siblings — so without
     dissolving that wrapper the buy box cannot be reordered against the
     gallery at all. Splitting .detail-info into two divs would work too,
     and would add a third child to a `3fr 2fr` grid, breaking every
     desktop product page.

     ⚠️ EVERY CHILD NEEDS AN EXPLICIT order, AND order TAKES AN INTEGER.
     Default order is 0, so one unlisted element silently jumps to the top.
     The catch-all sets 10 first; the named rules then pull eight elements
     forward. A fractional value (order: 8.5) is invalid — the declaration
     is dropped and that element falls back to 0, i.e. to the very top. */
  .detail-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 118px 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  .detail-info   { display: contents; }

  /* ⚠️ .detail-gallery IS A CHILD OF .detail-layout, NOT OF .detail-info,
     so the rule beneath does not reach it. Without this line the gallery
     auto-placed into column one and the product photo was squeezed into
     the 118px stepper column — 89px tall. It is also what made an earlier
     `auto` first column measure 247px: the track was sizing itself to the
     gallery rather than to the stepper. */
  .detail-layout > * { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .detail-info > *   { grid-column: 1 / -1; order: 10; }

  .detail-gallery   { order: 1; }
  .detail-badges    { order: 2; }
  .product-brand    { order: 3; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .detail-title     { order: 4; }
  .detail-price-row { order: 5; }
  .detail-shipping  { order: 6; }
  .pdp-trust-bar    { order: 9; }

  /* ── THE BUY ROW: STEPPER BESIDE THE BUTTON, ONE LINE AT ANY WIDTH ──
     .detail-ctas is dissolved too, so the add-to-cart form can take the
     second column while the wishlist button stays full width beneath it.
     Without that, everything inside .detail-ctas would be trapped in one
     column together.

     ⚠️ COLUMN ONE IS 118px, NOT `auto`. With `auto` the track sized itself
     from items SPANNING both columns rather than from the stepper, and on
     the live page the stepper came out 247px wide while Add to Cart was
     squeezed to 101px with its label wrapped onto three lines. A fixed
     118px is the stepper's natural width and leaves the button the rest,
     which is what makes the row hold at any screen size.

     ⚠️ :not(.bis) MATTERS. On out-of-stock pages the back-in-stock capture
     form is also a child of .detail-ctas; without the exclusion it would be
     pulled into the narrow second column instead of spanning the width. */
  .detail-ctas      { display: contents; }
  .detail-ctas > *  { grid-column: 1 / -1; order: 8; }
  .detail-qty       { grid-column: 1; order: 7; margin: 0; width: auto; }
  .detail-ctas > form:not(.bis) { grid-column: 2; order: 7; margin: 0; }
  .detail-ctas > form:not(.bis) .btn { height: 100%; }

  /* ⚠️ THE HERO KEEPS ITS FULL 4:3 SIZE. A draft shrank it to 3:2 to buy
     30px and the owner pushed back — on a product sold by appearance, the
     viewer is the page. Measured at full size the trust row still finishes
     at 843 against an 844 fold, so the space was never needed, and the
     thumbnail strip stays for the same reason. */
  .gallery-main { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .detail-sku  { order: 10; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .detail-rule { display: none; }
  .detail-price-row, .detail-shipping { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* ── PRICE, WAS-PRICE AND SAVINGS BADGE ON ONE LINE AT ANY WIDTH ─────
     clamp() scales all three with the viewport instead of wrapping, so
     the savings never drops to a second row and never has to be hunted
     for. Measured on the live page: 390px gives 24.2 / 12.5 / 10.2px and
     the row totals 281 of 358 available; 320px gives 21 / 12.3 / 10.2 and
     totals 264 of 288. Both fit with room.

     ⚠️ THE clamp() FLOORS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT LOWER. A first pass used
     .58rem for the badge and it rendered at 8.96px on a 320px phone —
     technically on one line, practically unreadable. The floors are the
     smallest sizes that still read; below them the badge should wrap
     rather than shrink. */
  .detail-price-row { flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 7px; align-items: baseline; }
  .detail-price { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 6.2vw, 1.95rem); white-space: nowrap; }
  .detail-was   { font-size: clamp(.82rem, 3.2vw, 1rem);    white-space: nowrap; }
  .detail-save  { font-size: clamp(.68rem, 2.6vw, .75rem);  white-space: nowrap;
                  padding: 3px 6px; flex: 0 0 auto; }

  /* All three trust statements on one row. At the inherited size they
     wrapped onto two, costing 32px and reading as a list rather than as a
     reassurance strip. */
  .pdp-trust-bar { flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 8px; font-size: .68rem; }
  .pdp-trust-bar .ptb-item { white-space: nowrap; gap: 4px; }
  .pdp-trust-bar svg { width: 13px; height: 13px; flex: 0 0 auto; }

  /* The SKU and the Google rating sat ~30px apart for no reason. */
  .pdp-google-rating { margin: 2px 0 0; }

  /* ── 1. THUMBNAILS: ONE SCROLLING ROW, NOT A TWO-ROW GRID  (-224px) ──
     The grid is overridden rather than removed: display:flex wins over
     display:grid, and grid-template-columns is reset so a future edit to
     the desktop rule cannot leak a column count into the scroller. */
  .detail-gallery .gallery-thumbs {
    display: flex;
    grid-template-columns: none;
    gap: 6px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: x proximity;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .detail-gallery .gallery-thumb {
    flex: 0 0 56px;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    aspect-ratio: auto;      /* the desktop rule sets 1; flex-basis owns it now */
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }
  /* Past the sixth image the markup adds .thumb-hidden and renders a
     "See N more" button. In a horizontal scroller both are pointless —
     swiping IS the reveal — so every thumb is shown and the button goes.
     Hiding the button rather than removing it keeps the JS handler
     harmless: it simply never fires. */
  .detail-gallery .gallery-thumb.thumb-hidden { display: block; }
  .detail-gallery .gallery-seemore-btn        { display: none; }

  /* ── 2. TITLE: TWO LINES, NOT FOUR  (-70px) ──────────────────────────
     line-clamp is VISUAL ONLY — the full product name stays in the DOM,
     so the h1 Google reads is unchanged, as are <title>, the meta
     description and the Product JSON-LD. */
  .detail-title {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── 3. BREADCRUMB: GONE ON PHONES  (-44px) ──────────────────────────
     The approved mockup has no breadcrumb in the proposed frame, and it is
     right: the back gesture does that job on a phone, and two lines of
     "Home > Bathroom Vanities- All > <the whole product name again>" buy
     nothing in the opening screen. display:none, not removed — the markup
     and its BreadcrumbList structured data stay intact for Google and for
     every width above the mobile band. */
  .breadcrumb { display: none; }
}
</style>

<%# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    PRODUCT-EXPERT CALL — ITS OWN BLOCK, AND DELIBERATELY SO.

    The block above is mobile-only by construction and a gate asserts that
    every rule in it sits inside the media query. This control renders at
    every width, so its rules cannot live there without breaking that
    guarantee — and the guarantee is worth more than the tidiness of one
    style element.
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ %>
<style nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
  /* ⚠️ nowrap IS THE POINT, NOT A TIDY-UP. This was flex-wrap:wrap, which
     is how the phone icon ended up stranded on a line of its own above the
     words: the contents overflowed by 15px at 375px and wrap silently
     relocated the glyph instead of showing anything was wrong. The button
     rendered 73px tall on the live site and nothing failed.

     With nowrap, contents that no longer fit overflow visibly instead of
     quietly rearranging themselves, so the next person to lengthen this
     label sees it immediately. gate_pdp_mobile_fold measures the label
     against the button at 320, 360 and 375 and fails if it no longer
     clears. The label text carries its own measurements where it lives. */
  .pdp-expert-cta {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px; width: 100%; text-align: center; flex-wrap: nowrap;
  }
  .pdp-expert-hours {
    font-size: .76rem; color: #777; text-align: center; margin: 6px 0 0;
  }
  /* The number is hidden on phones, where the control is already one tap
     to dial, and shown from the tablet band up, where a tel: link may hand
     off to an app the visitor does not have. The band comes from the same
     resolved settings as everything else — never a typed literal. */
  .pdp-expert-num { display: none; font-weight: 700; }
  @media <%= _bpPdp.mq.tabletAndUp %> {
    .pdp-expert-num { display: inline; }
  }
</style>

<!-- Breadcrumb -->
<div class="breadcrumb">
  <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo;
  <% if (category) { %><a href="/collections/<%= category.slug %>"><%= category.name %></a> &rsaquo;<% } %>
  <span><%= product.name %></span>
</div>

<!-- ── Product Detail Layout ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="detail-layout">

  <!-- ── Gallery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <%
    const _imgs  = product.images || [];
    const _shown = _imgs.slice(0, 6);
    const _total = _imgs.length;
    // Indices that span the full gallery width (hero rows)
    const _heroIdx = new Set([0, 3]);
    const _badgeLabel = { sale: 'SALE', new: 'NEW', best: 'BEST SELLER' };
  %>
  <div class="detail-gallery" id="pdp-gallery">

    <!-- Main image viewer -->
    <div class="gallery-main" id="gallery-main"
         role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="View full-size image"
         data-pdp="open">
      <img class="gallery-main-img" id="gallery-main-img"
           src="<%= (_imgs[0]||{}).url||'' %>"
           alt="<%= (_imgs[0]||{}).alt_text || product.name %>"
           loading="eager" draggable="false">
      <% if (product.badge && _badgeLabel[product.badge]) { %>
      <span class="gallery-badge"><%= _badgeLabel[product.badge] %></span>
      <% } %>
      <span class="gallery-main-zoom" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2"><path d="M15 3h6v6M9 21H3v-6M21 3l-7 7M3 21l7-7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Thumbnail grid: 3 per row, 2 rows shown, expand for more -->
    <% if (_total > 1) { %>
    <div class="gallery-thumbs-wrap">
      <div class="gallery-thumbs" id="gallery-thumbs">
        <% _imgs.forEach(function(img, idx) { %>
        <button class="gallery-thumb<%= idx===0?' is-active':'' %><%= idx>=6?' thumb-hidden':'' %>"
                type="button" data-idx="<%= idx %>"
                aria-label="Image <%= idx+1 %><%= _total > 1 ? ' of ' + _total : '' %>"
                data-pdp="thumb">
          <img src="<%= img.url %>" alt="<%= img.alt_text || product.name %>" loading="lazy" draggable="false">
        </button>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
      <% if (_total > 6) { %>
      <button class="gallery-seemore-btn" id="gallery-seemore-btn" type="button"
              data-pdp="more">
        See <%= _total - 6 %> more &#8595;
      </button>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <% } %>

    <!-- ── Lightbox ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <style nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
      /* The bundle makes .lb-stage a 920px-wide flex box that centres its
         child. Both fight a transform-driven viewer, so neutralise them:
         the stage becomes a plain positioned window, the image is placed
         absolutely, and one transform does all the work. */
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-stage{display:block;position:relative;max-width:none;
        width:100%;padding:0;margin:52px 0 6px;overflow:hidden;touch-action:none;
        cursor:zoom-in;background:transparent}
      /* Cursor states the affordance: a magnifier while another zoom rung is
         still available, the hand only once we are at 100% and panning is
         the thing left to do. */
      #pdp-lightbox.at-max .lb-stage{cursor:zoom-out}
      #pdp-lightbox.at-max.can-pan .lb-stage{cursor:grab}
      #pdp-lightbox.is-panning .lb-stage{cursor:grabbing}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-img{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;max-width:none;
        max-height:none;transform-origin:0 0;will-change:transform;
        border-radius:0;user-select:none;-webkit-user-drag:none}

      /* Arrows sat top-right under the close button. Centre them vertically. */
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-arrow{top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);bottom:auto}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-prev{left:14px;right:auto}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-next{right:14px;left:auto}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-close{top:14px;right:14px;z-index:4}

      #pdp-lightbox .lb-zoom{position:absolute;top:14px;left:14px;z-index:4;
        display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2px;
        background:rgba(0,0,0,.55);border-radius:6px;padding:4px 6px}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-zoom button{background:transparent;border:0;color:#fff;
        font:600 15px/1 system-ui,sans-serif;padding:5px 9px;border-radius:4px;cursor:pointer}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-zoom button:hover:not(:disabled){background:rgba(255,255,255,.16)}
      #pdp-lightbox .lb-zoom button:disabled{opacity:.3;cursor:default}
      #pdp-lightbox #lb-zoom-reset{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.02em}
      #pdp-lightbox #lb-zoom-pct{color:#fff;font:600 12px/1 system-ui,sans-serif;
        min-width:46px;text-align:center;opacity:.85}
      @media (max-width:640px){
        #pdp-lightbox .lb-stage{margin:48px 0 4px}
        #pdp-lightbox .lb-zoom{top:auto;bottom:100px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%)}
        #pdp-lightbox .lb-arrow{display:none}
      }
    </style>

    <div class="gallery-lightbox" id="pdp-lightbox"
         role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Product image gallery" hidden>
      <button class="lb-close" data-pdp="lb-close" aria-label="Close gallery" type="button">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
      <button class="lb-arrow lb-prev" data-pdp="lb-prev" aria-label="Previous image" type="button">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="15 18 9 12 15 6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="lb-stage" id="lb-stage">
        <img class="lb-img" id="lb-img" src="" alt="" draggable="false">
      </div>
      <div class="lb-zoom" id="lb-zoom" aria-hidden="false">
        <button type="button" id="lb-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">&minus;</button>
        <span id="lb-zoom-pct">100%</span>
        <button type="button" id="lb-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
        <button type="button" id="lb-zoom-reset" aria-label="Reset zoom">Reset</button>
      </div>
      <button class="lb-arrow lb-next" data-pdp="lb-next" aria-label="Next image" type="button">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="lb-footer">
        <p class="lb-counter" id="lb-counter" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="lb-thumbs" id="lb-thumbs">
          <% _imgs.forEach((img, idx) => { %>
          <button class="lb-thumb" data-idx="<%= idx %>"
                  data-pdp="lb-goto" type="button"
                  aria-label="Image <%= idx + 1 %>">
            <img src="<%= img.url %>?width=160" data-full="<%= img.url %>"
                 alt="<%= img.alt_text || product.name %>" loading="lazy">
          </button>
          <% }); %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  <script nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
  var pdpGallery = (function(){
    var _allImgs = <%- JSON.stringify(_imgs.map(function(i){return{url:i.url||'',alt:i.alt_text||''};})) %>;
    var _active = 0;
    function select(idx) {
      _active = idx;
      var el = document.getElementById('gallery-main-img');
      if (el) { el.src = _allImgs[idx].url; el.alt = _allImgs[idx].alt; }
      document.querySelectorAll('.gallery-thumb').forEach(function(t, i) {
        t.classList.toggle('is-active', i === idx);
      });
    }
    function showMore(btn) {
      document.querySelectorAll('#gallery-thumbs .thumb-hidden').forEach(function(t) {
        t.classList.remove('thumb-hidden');
        t.style.display = '';
      });
      if (btn) btn.style.display = 'none';
    }
    function getActive() { return _active; }
    return { select: select, showMore: showMore, getActive: getActive };
  })();
  </script>


  <script nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
  /* PDP zoom viewer.
     Runs on DOMContentLoaded — after site.js parses at the end of <body> —
     so it replaces the window.pdpLightbox site.js installs. Same API
     (open/close/prev/next/goTo), so the inline onclick handlers still work.

     Model: the image is absolutely placed at 0,0 with transform-origin 0 0.
     One transform — translate(tx,ty) scale(s) — is the only thing that
     positions it. `fit` is the scale at which the whole image is visible;
     scale 1 is the file's own pixels. Nothing else centres anything. */
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var box = document.getElementById('pdp-lightbox');
    if (!box) return;
    var stage = document.getElementById('lb-stage'),
        img   = document.getElementById('lb-img'),
        pct   = document.getElementById('lb-zoom-pct'),
        cnt   = document.getElementById('lb-counter'),
        bIn   = document.getElementById('lb-zoom-in'),
        bOut  = document.getElementById('lb-zoom-out'),
        bRes  = document.getElementById('lb-zoom-reset'),
        thumbs= Array.prototype.slice.call(box.querySelectorAll('.lb-thumb')),
        n     = thumbs.length;

    var cur = 0, fit = 1, scale = 1, tx = 0, ty = 0, ready = false;
    var MAXF = 1;                       // 1 = stop at the file's native pixels

    function vw() { return stage.clientWidth; }
    function vh() { return stage.clientHeight; }

    function draw() {
      var w = img.naturalWidth * scale, h = img.naturalHeight * scale;
      tx = w <= vw() ? (vw() - w) / 2 : Math.min(0, Math.max(vw() - w, tx));
      ty = h <= vh() ? (vh() - h) / 2 : Math.min(0, Math.max(vh() - h, ty));
      img.style.transform = 'translate(' + tx + 'px,' + ty + 'px) scale(' + scale + ')';
      pct.textContent = Math.round(scale * 100) + '%';
      var zoomed = scale > fit * 1.001;
      box.classList.toggle('is-zoomed', zoomed);
      box.classList.toggle('at-max', scale >= MAXF * 0.999);
      box.classList.toggle('can-pan', w > vw() + 1 || h > vh() + 1);
      bOut.disabled = scale <= fit * 1.001;
      bIn.disabled  = scale >= MAXF * 0.999;
      bRes.disabled = !zoomed;
    }

    function reset() {
      if (!img.naturalWidth) return;
      ready = true;
      fit = Math.min(vw() / img.naturalWidth, vh() / img.naturalHeight, 1);
      scale = fit; tx = 0; ty = 0;
      draw();
    }

    /* zoom keeping the point under the cursor fixed */
    function zoomTo(next, cx, cy) {
      if (!ready) return;
      next = Math.min(MAXF, Math.max(fit, next));
      if (Math.abs(next - scale) < 0.0005) return;
      var r = stage.getBoundingClientRect();
      var ax = (cx - r.left - tx) / scale, ay = (cy - r.top - ty) / scale;
      tx = (cx - r.left) - ax * next;
      ty = (cy - r.top)  - ay * next;
      scale = next;
      draw();
    }
    function centre() { var r = stage.getBoundingClientRect();
                        return [r.left + r.width / 2, r.top + r.height / 2]; }

    function show(i) {
      cur = ((i % n) + n) % n;
      var t = thumbs[cur], im = t && t.querySelector('img');
      if (!im) return;
      ready = false;
      img.style.transform = 'translate(0,0) scale(0)';   // hide until measured
      img.src = im.getAttribute('data-full') || im.src;  // native file, never resized
      img.alt = im.alt || '';
      if (cnt) cnt.textContent = (cur + 1) + ' / ' + n;
      thumbs.forEach(function (x) { x.classList.remove('active'); });
      t.classList.add('active');
      t.scrollIntoView({ inline: 'nearest', block: 'nearest' });
      if (img.complete && img.naturalWidth) reset();     // cached: load won't fire
    }
    img.addEventListener('load', reset);

    var api = {
      open:  function (i) { box.removeAttribute('hidden');
                            document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
                            show(i || 0);
                            requestAnimationFrame(function(){ if (ready) reset(); }); },
      close: function () { box.setAttribute('hidden', '');
                           document.body.style.overflow = '';
                           box.classList.remove('is-zoomed','at-max','is-panning','can-pan'); },
      prev:  function () { show(cur - 1); },
      next:  function () { show(cur + 1); },
      goTo:  function (i) { show(i); }
    };
    window.pdpLightbox = api;

    bIn .addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.stopPropagation(); var c = centre(); zoomTo(scale * 1.5, c[0], c[1]); });
    bOut.addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.stopPropagation(); var c = centre(); zoomTo(scale / 1.5, c[0], c[1]); });
    bRes.addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.stopPropagation(); scale = fit; tx = 0; ty = 0; draw(); });

    stage.addEventListener('wheel', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      zoomTo(scale * (e.deltaY < 0 ? 1.18 : 1 / 1.18), e.clientX, e.clientY);
    }, { passive: false });

    /* Click ladder: fit -> mid -> full, then back to fit.
       `mid` is the geometric mean of fit and full, so each click feels like
       the same jump. If the image is small enough that mid and full are
       within a few percent, the ladder collapses to two rungs. */
    function steps() {
      var mid = Math.sqrt(fit * MAXF);
      return (MAXF / fit < 1.6 || mid / fit < 1.25 || MAXF / mid < 1.25)
        ? [fit, MAXF] : [fit, mid, MAXF];
    }
    function nextStep() {
      var st = steps();
      for (var i = 0; i < st.length; i++) {
        if (scale < st[i] * 0.995) return st[i];     // first rung above us
      }
      return st[0];                                   // at the top: back to fit
    }
    var moved = false;
    stage.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      if (moved) { moved = false; return; }          // that was a drag, not a click
      var next = nextStep();
      if (next === fit) { scale = fit; tx = 0; ty = 0; draw(); }
      else { zoomTo(next, e.clientX, e.clientY); }
    });

    var pts = {}, last = null, pinch = 0;
    function keys() { return Object.keys(pts); }
    function dist() { var k = keys(); if (k.length < 2) return 0;
                      var a = pts[k[0]], b = pts[k[1]];
                      return Math.hypot(a.x - b.x, a.y - b.y); }
    function mid()  { var k = keys(), a = pts[k[0]], b = pts[k[1]];
                      return { x: (a.x + b.x) / 2, y: (a.y + b.y) / 2 }; }

    stage.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (e) {
      stage.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
      pts[e.pointerId] = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY };
      if (keys().length === 1) { last = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY }; moved = false; }
      if (keys().length === 2) pinch = dist();
    });
    stage.addEventListener('pointermove', function (e) {
      if (!pts[e.pointerId]) return;
      pts[e.pointerId] = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY };
      if (keys().length === 2 && pinch) {
        var d = dist(), m = mid();
        zoomTo(scale * (d / pinch), m.x, m.y);
        pinch = d; moved = true; return;
      }
      if (keys().length === 1 && last && box.classList.contains('can-pan')) {
        var dx = e.clientX - last.x, dy = e.clientY - last.y;
        if (Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) > 3) { moved = true; box.classList.add('is-panning'); }
        tx += dx; ty += dy;
        last = { x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY };
        draw();
      }
    });
    function release(e) {
      delete pts[e.pointerId];
      if (!keys().length) { last = null; pinch = 0; box.classList.remove('is-panning'); }
    }
    stage.addEventListener('pointerup', release);
    stage.addEventListener('pointercancel', release);

    box.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === box) api.close(); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
      if (box.hasAttribute('hidden')) return;
      var c;
      if (e.key === 'Escape')     api.close();
      if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft')  api.prev();
      if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') api.next();
      if (e.key === '+' || e.key === '=') { c = centre(); zoomTo(scale * 1.5, c[0], c[1]); }
      if (e.key === '-' || e.key === '_') { c = centre(); zoomTo(scale / 1.5, c[0], c[1]); }
      if (e.key === '0') { scale = fit; tx = 0; ty = 0; draw(); }
    });
    window.addEventListener('resize', function () { if (!box.hasAttribute('hidden')) reset(); });
  });
  </script>

  </div><!-- /detail-gallery -->

  <!-- ── Product info ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="detail-info">

    <!-- Badges -->
    <div class="detail-badges">
      <% if (product.badge === 'sale')  { %><span class="product-badge badge-sale">SALE</span><% } %>
      <% if (product.badge === 'new')   { %><span class="product-badge badge-new">NEW</span><% } %>
      <% if (product.badge === 'best')  { %><span class="product-badge badge-best">BEST SELLER</span><% } %>
      <% if (!product.inStock)          { %><span class="product-badge" style="background:#7A7264">OUT OF STOCK</span><% } %>
    </div>

    <% if (product.brand) { %><p class="product-brand" style="margin-bottom:6px"><%= product.brand %></p><% } %>
    <%# ⚠️ THE HEADING IS THE ONLY PLACE THE SHORTENED TITLE APPEARS.
         src/utils/displayTitle.js trims James Martin vanity names of
         "Single Hole", "3 CM" and "& Backsplash" — all of which remain in
         the specifications table below. Everything else on this page and on
         every collection card keeps product.name: the <title>, the meta
         description, the Product JSON-LD and the breadcrumb trail. Search
         listings are therefore unchanged.

         Anything outside James Martin vanities comes back untouched, as do
         names where the result fails the safety checks in that file. %>
    <h1 class="detail-title"><%= displayTitle(product.name, product) %></h1>
    <p class="detail-sku">SKU: <%= product.sku %></p>

    <%# ── PRODUCT REVIEW FIGURE ──────────────────────────────────────────
         The same figure and the same treatment the collection pages use —
         src/services/jmvReviewService.forModel(). It sits ABOVE the price
         because that is where a rating belongs: it is the reason the price
         is worth considering, not a footnote to it.

         ⚠️ NOTHING HERE GOES INTO STRUCTURED DATA, EVER. These are reviews
         collected by Home Depot and Ferguson, not by us. Google requires
         review markup to describe the site's own reviews, and
         gates/gate_structured_data.js asserts that no aggregateRating or
         review itemprop appears on this page. The figure is shown to a
         human and withheld from the crawler, deliberately.

         ⚠️ THE ATTRIBUTION LINE IS NOT DECORATION. "at national retailers"
         is what keeps the claim honest — without it the page implies these
         are our reviews. It renders with the figure or not at all.

         forModel() returns null when the rules refuse the figure — too few
         reviews, too wide a spread between retailers, or an unpublished
         row — and null renders nothing rather than a placeholder. %>
    <% if (jmvReview) { %>
    <section class="jmv-rev jmv-rev--pdp">
      <div class="jmv-rev-top">
        <span class="jmv-rev-score"><%= jmvReview.ratingText %></span>
        <%# Partial fill by PERCENTAGE, never a rounded count of solid stars:
            4.3 drawn as five full stars is a false claim. aria-hidden
            because the accessible value is the text beside it. %>
        <span class="jmv-rev-stars" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="jmv-rev-track">★★★★★</span>
          <span class="jmv-rev-fill" style="width:<%= jmvReview.fillPct.toFixed(1) %>%">★★★★★</span>
        </span>
        <span class="jmv-rev-count">· <%= jmvReview.count.toLocaleString('en-US') %> reviews</span>
      </div>
      <p class="jmv-rev-src">Average across verified customer reviews at national
        retailers<% if (jmvReview.verifiedOn) { %>, <%= jmvReview.verifiedOn %><% } %>.</p>
    </section>
    <% } %>

    <!-- Price -->
    <div class="detail-price-row">
      <span class="detail-price">$<%= product.price.toLocaleString('en-US', {minimumFractionDigits:2}) %></span>
      <% if (product.compare_price && product.compare_price > product.price) { %>
      <span class="detail-was">$<%= product.compare_price.toLocaleString('en-US', {minimumFractionDigits:2}) %></span>
      <span class="detail-save">Save $<%= product.savings %></span>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <p class="detail-shipping">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="1" y="3" width="15" height="13" rx="1"/>
        <path d="M16 8h4l3 3v5h-7V8z"/><circle cx="5.5" cy="18.5" r="2.5"/><circle cx="18.5" cy="18.5" r="2.5"/>
      </svg>
      Free shipping — arrives in 5–10 business days
    </p>

    <hr class="detail-rule">

    <!-- Short description -->
    <% if (product.short_desc) { %>
    <p class="detail-short-desc"><%= product.short_desc %></p>
    <hr class="detail-rule">
    <% } %>

    <!-- Qty stepper -->
    <div class="detail-qty" role="group" aria-label="Quantity">
      <button class="qty-btn" type="button" aria-label="Decrease quantity" data-qty-step="-1">−</button>
      <span class="qty-val" id="qty-val">1</span>
      <button class="qty-btn" type="button" aria-label="Increase quantity" data-qty-step="1">+</button>
    </div>

    <!-- CTAs -->
    <div class="detail-ctas">
      <form action="/cart/add" method="POST">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="product_id" value="<%= product.id %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="slug"        value="<%= product.slug %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="name"        value="<%= product.name %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="price"       value="<%= product.price %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="image"       value="<%= (product.images[0]||{}).url||'' %>">
        <input type="hidden" name="qty"         id="atc-qty" value="1">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-amber" <%= !product.inStock ? 'disabled' : '' %> style="width:100%">
          <%= product.inStock ? 'Add to Cart' : 'Out of Stock' %>
        </button>
      </form>

      <%# ── CALL A PRODUCT EXPERT ──────────────────────────────────────────
           A $2,400 vanity is not an impulse buy, and the questions that stop
           one — will it fit, is the finish what the photo shows, what does
           delivery actually involve — are answered in two minutes by a person
           and not at all by a spec table.

           ⚠️ A DIRECT CALL, NOT A BOOKING. Owner decision: a scheduler means
           a calendar, a notification path and a dashboard to build, and it
           makes somebody who is ready NOW wait until Tuesday. tel: is one tap
           on the device where the hesitation is happening.

           ⚠️ IN-STOCK PAGES ONLY. Owner decision, from the two options in
           docs/mockups/expert_cta_out_of_stock_options.html. On an
           out-of-stock page the back-in-stock capture form is the one ask,
           and it exists precisely because those pages were dead ends —
           putting a second call-to-action beside it makes the shopper choose
           between leaving an address and making a call, with neither clearly
           primary.

           ⚠️ IT RENDERS ONLY WHEN THERE IS A NUMBER TO CALL. contact_phone is
           blank until it is filled in at Theme Editor > Global. A "call us"
           control that dials nothing is worse than no control, so the absence
           of the setting removes it rather than rendering it dead. %>
      <% var _expertPhone = String(((settings || {}).global || {}).contact_phone || '').trim(); %>
      <% if (product.inStock && _expertPhone) { %>
      <%# ⚠️ NO ICON, AND THE LABEL IS SHORT ON PURPOSE. BOTH ARE MEASUREMENTS,
           NOT TASTE. The button's usable inner width is roughly the viewport
           minus 92px, and the original label "Questions? Call a product
           expert." needs 274px:

             375px iPhone  → 283px available → fits by 9px
             360px Android → 268px available → does NOT fit
             320px phone   → 228px available → does not fit at any font size

           With a 16px icon and its 8px gap the line needed 298px, so it
           overflowed even the 375px case and flex-wrap dropped the icon onto
           a row of its own — a 73px-tall button with the glyph stranded
           above the words. That was live on the site and is what prompted
           this.

           "Questions? Call an expert." measures 213px, which clears the
           narrowest phone by 15px. Re-adding the icon costs 24px and puts
           it back over at 320px (237 > 228), so the icon cannot come back
           without the wrap coming back with it. Lengthening the label has
           the same effect: "Questions? Call our experts." was measured at
           233px and misses 320px by 5px. Measure before changing either. %>
      <a class="btn btn-outline pdp-expert-cta"
         href="tel:<%= _expertPhone.replace(/[^0-9+]/g, '') %>"
         data-pdp="expert-call">
        <span>Questions? Call an expert.</span>
        <%# The number is shown as TEXT on desktop and hidden on phones, where
            the whole control is already one tap to dial. A tel: link on a
            laptop hands off to FaceTime or a dialer the visitor may not have,
            so the number itself has to be readable there. %>
        <span class="pdp-expert-num"><%= _expertPhone %></span>
      </a>
      <p class="pdp-expert-hours">Available 9am&ndash;5:30pm ET, Mon&ndash;Sat</p>
      <% } %>

      <%# ── BACK IN STOCK CAPTURE ─────────────────────────────────────────
           Out-of-stock pages only. 20% of the feed (1,178 of 5,873) is out of
           stock, 725 of them in the largest category, and until this existed
           every one of those pages was a dead end: a disabled button, a
           wishlist link, and cross-sells to four different models. The person
           who wanted THIS vanity left and we learned nothing.

           ⚠️ THE OPT-IN BOX IS UNTICKED AND MUST STAY UNTICKED. A pre-ticked
           box re-subscribing somebody who previously opted out is the fastest
           route to spam complaints, and Brevo scores complaint rate at the
           ACCOUNT level — the same account that delivers order confirmations
           for $5,000 freight orders. Owner decision 2026-11-09, after
           explicitly considering the pre-ticked version and rejecting it. %>
      <% if (!product.inStock) { %>
        <form class="bis" action="/notify-me" method="POST" data-bis>
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf"      value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <input type="hidden" name="product_id" value="<%= product.id %>">
          <input type="hidden" name="sku"        value="<%= product.sku %>">
          <%# Honeypot. Real people leave it empty; bots fill everything in.
              Hidden from assistive tech too, so nobody is asked to skip it. %>
          <input type="text" name="company" class="bis-hp" tabindex="-1"
                 autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true">

          <p class="bis-lead">Email me when this is back in stock</p>
          <div class="bis-row">
            <label class="bis-sr" for="bis-email-<%= product.id %>">Email address</label>
            <input type="email" id="bis-email-<%= product.id %>" name="email"
                   placeholder="your@email.com" required autocomplete="email">
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-amber bis-go">Notify me</button>
          </div>
          <label class="bis-opt">
            <input type="checkbox" name="marketing_opt_in">
            <span>Also send me occasional updates on similar vanities</span>
          </label>
          <p class="bis-fine">We'll email you once, when this item is back. Nothing else.</p>
          <%# Shown immediately on the no-JS path, where /notify-me redirects
               back here with ?notified=1. With JS the same line is revealed in
               place by site.js without reloading. %>
          <p class="bis-done" <%= (query && query.notified) ? '' : 'hidden' %>>Done — we'll email you the moment it's back.</p>
        </form>
      <% } %>

      <button type="button"
              class="btn btn-outline heart-btn heart-btn--pdp<%= isFavorited ? ' is-saved' : '' %>"
              data-product-id="<%= product.id %>"
              data-product-slug="<%= product.slug %>"
              style="width:100%;text-align:center"
              aria-label="<%= isFavorited ? 'Remove from saved items' : 'Save to favorites' %>">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" width="16" height="16" style="vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M20.84 4.61a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.78 0L12 5.67l-1.06-1.06a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.78 7.78l1.06 1.06L12 21.23l7.78-7.78 1.06-1.06a5.5 5.5 0 0 0 0-7.78z"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="heart-btn-label"><%= isFavorited ? 'Saved' : 'Save to Wishlist' %></span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Trust signals ─────────────────────────────────────────────
